; ==========================================================================
; STELLAR MORSE RECEIVER v10  -  key it on the Input switch   (loads at $4000, VM1)
; ==========================================================================
; Load, cold-boot, tell it roughly how fast you key (5-25 WPM, Enter = 12), then
; key Morse on the Elf2K's Input switch (EF4). Each letter appears on the terminal
; (and the hex display) as you finish it; a longer pause is a word space. Q follows
; the key - a sidetone if a sounder is on Q. Q or ESC on the terminal quits.
;
; IT LEARNS YOUR HAND: running averages of your dots and dashes decide dot or dash,
; and separate averages of YOUR gaps - inside a letter, between letters, between
; words - decide where letters and words end (never later than 2.75 of your current
; dots for a letter, and between 4.5 and 6.5 dots for a word). The first six marks
; are learned at double speed. The learning runs as native 1802 code ($4300, via
; $F1 RUNMC) straight after each release, so the key is watched again in ~9 ms.
;
; Limits found in testing: if you key much FASTER than you told it (a third faster)
; the first letter or two may come out wrong while it learns; a very uneven hand at
; 18+ WPM can split a letter now and then. Best at 5-20 WPM.
;
; NEEDS the GETEFA mask patch (Firmware-Math/GETEFA-mask-fix.dlines.txt): the key is read as
; bit 3 of GETEFA's EF mask (TESTBITI 08). On firmware without it, use the July receivers.
;
; VERIFICATION (Firmware-Math/morse_rx_verify.py, V0061.34 + GETEFA mask): 8/8 PASS (12/20/8 WPM, jitter, a sloppy hand, drift, digits+punctuation, a long message, rerun)
; NOT YET RUN ON HARDWARE.
;
; 194 STELLAR commands (+ the native learning step).
;
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DISASSEMBLY  -  commented out; the loader skips it
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

; D 4000 CD             START
; D 4001 11 0F 00 0A    LOADXI R15 000A
; D 4005 11 0B 00 00    LOADXI R11 0000
; D 4009 0A 00          SETQ 00
; D 400B 11 0E 07 80    LOADXI R14 0780
; D 400F C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; ASK:
; D 4011 11 0E 08 3F    LOADXI R14 083F
; D 4015 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 4017 11 0C 0A 00    LOADXI R12 0A00
; D 401B 11 0D 0A 00    LOADXI R13 0A00
; D 401F C2 CD          GETSTR R12 R13                     the number
; D 4021 11 07 00 00    LOADXI R7 0000
; D 4025 11 04 00 00    LOADXI R4 0000
; DIG:
; D 4029 2E 04 0A 00    READIDX R4 0A00                    next character
; D 402D 21 0A          COPYAX Acc -> R10
; D 402F 8C 0A          TESTXZ R10
; D 4031 A0 00 56       IFTRUEI DGD
; D 4034 11 09 00 30    LOADXI R9 0030
; D 4038 89 A9          TESTLXY R10 < R9
; D 403A A0 00 11       IFTRUEI ASK                        not a digit: ask again
; D 403D 11 09 00 3A    LOADXI R9 003A
; D 4041 88 A9          TESTGXY R10 >= R9
; D 4043 A0 00 11       IFTRUEI ASK
; D 4046 53 0A 00 30    SUBXI R10 0030
; D 404A 4A 7F          MULTXY R7 * R15
; D 404C 21 17          COPYAX MA -> R7                    W x 10
; D 404E 50 7A 07       ADDXYZ R7 + R10 -> R7              + the digit
; D 4051 42 04          INCX R4
; D 4053 B0 00 29       GAL DIG
; DGD:
; D 4056 8C 07          TESTXZ R7
; D 4058 A1 00 5F       IFFALSEI HAVE
; D 405B 11 07 00 0C    LOADXI R7 000C                     Enter alone: 12
; HAVE:
; D 405F 11 09 00 05    LOADXI R9 0005
; D 4063 89 79          TESTLXY R7 < R9
; D 4065 A0 00 11       IFTRUEI ASK
; D 4068 11 09 00 1A    LOADXI R9 001A
; D 406C 88 79          TESTGXY R7 >= R9
; D 406E A0 00 11       IFTRUEI ASK
; D 4071 11 0E 08 81    LOADXI R14 0881
; D 4075 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14                       printed FIRST: PRINTSTR uses RE, which then holds a gap average
; D 4077 11 01 00 6A    LOADXI R1 006A
; D 407B 23 00 7A       COPYXY R7 -> R10
; D 407E 11 09 00 02    LOADXI R9 0002
; D 4082 4D A9          DIVXY R10 / R9
; D 4084 25             COPYMAA
; D 4085 21 09          COPYAX Acc -> R9
; D 4087 50 19 01       ADDXYZ R1 + R9 -> R1
; D 408A 4D 17          DIVXY R1 / R7
; D 408C 25             COPYMAA
; D 408D 21 01          COPYAX Acc -> R1                   dot = 106 / WPM samples, rounded
; D 408F 50 11 02       ADDXYZ R1 + R1 -> R2
; D 4092 50 21 02       ADDXYZ R2 + R1 -> R2               dash = 3 dots
; D 4095 50 11 0E       ADDXYZ R1 + R1 -> R14              gap in a letter: 1 dot (x2: the gap loop counts in twos)
; D 4098 50 EE 0F       ADDXYZ R14 + R14 -> R15
; D 409B 50 FE 0F       ADDXYZ R15 + R14 -> R15            3 dots (x2) ...
; D 409E 23 00 17       COPYXY R1 -> R7
; D 40A1 61 72          SHIFTBX R7 right 1
; D 40A3 50 F7 0F       ADDXYZ R15 + R7 -> R15             ... + a quarter dot: between letters 3.25 to start
; D 40A6 50 EE 07       ADDXYZ R14 + R14 -> R7
; D 40A9 50 77 07       ADDXYZ R7 + R7 -> R7
; D 40AC 50 77 07       ADDXYZ R7 + R7 -> R7
; D 40AF 51 7E 07       SUBXYZ R7 - R14 -> R7              between words: 7 dots (x2: 16 - 2 = 14)
; D 40B2 11 0A 0B 00    LOADXI R10 0B00
; D 40B6 3A 02 7A       COPYXMY R7 -> M(R10)
; D 40B9 11 07 00 00    LOADXI R7 0000
; D 40BD 52 0A 00 02    ADDXI R10 0002
; D 40C1 3A 02 7A       COPYXMY R7 -> M(R10)               no marks seen yet: learn fast for the first six
; D 40C4 50 12 03       ADDXYZ R1 + R2 -> R3               dot + dash
; D 40C7 50 EF 0C       ADDXYZ R14 + R15 -> R12
; D 40CA 61 C2          SHIFTBX R12 right 1                LETTER = midway: inside a letter / between letters
; D 40CC 11 0A 0B 00    LOADXI R10 0B00
; D 40D0 39 02 A9       COPYMXY M(R10) -> R9
; D 40D3 50 9F 09       ADDXYZ R9 + R15 -> R9
; D 40D6 61 92          SHIFTBX R9 right 1                 WORD = midway: between letters / words
; D 40D8 50 11 07       ADDXYZ R1 + R1 -> R7
; D 40DB 50 77 0A       ADDXYZ R7 + R7 -> R10              RA = 4 dots (x2)
; D 40DE 23 00 17       COPYXY R1 -> R7
; D 40E1 61 72          SHIFTBX R7 right 1
; D 40E3 50 71 07       ADDXYZ R7 + R1 -> R7
; D 40E6 50 7A 07       ADDXYZ R7 + R10 -> R7              5.5 (x2) = 2.75 dots
; D 40E9 89 7C          TESTLXY R7 < R12
; D 40EB A1 00 F1       IFFALSEI CL1s
; D 40EE 23 00 7C       COPYXY R7 -> R12
; CL1s:
; D 40F1 50 AA 07       ADDXYZ R10 + R10 -> R7
; D 40F4 50 71 07       ADDXYZ R7 + R1 -> R7               9 (x2) = 4.5 dots
; D 40F7 89 97          TESTLXY R9 < R7
; D 40F9 A1 00 FF       IFFALSEI CL2s
; D 40FC 23 00 79       COPYXY R7 -> R9
; CL2s:
; D 40FF 50 7A 07       ADDXYZ R7 + R10 -> R7              13 (x2) = 6.5 dots
; D 4102 89 79          TESTLXY R7 < R9
; D 4104 A1 01 0A       IFFALSEI CL3s
; D 4107 23 00 79       COPYXY R7 -> R9
; CL3s:
; D 410A 11 05 00 01    LOADXI R5 0001                     no elements yet
; D 410E 11 06 00 00    LOADXI R6 0000
; D 4112 11 08 00 00    LOADXI R8 0000
; UP:
; D 4116 11 04 00 00    LOADXI R4 0000
; UL:
; D 411A CC             SERST                              a key on the terminal?
; D 411B A0 01 8B       IFTRUEI TKEY
; D 411E 10 00 00       LOADAI 0000
; D 4121 09             GETEFA                             EF1-4 as a mask
; D 4122 1A 08          TESTBITI 08                        EF4: the Input switch
; D 4124 A0 01 5E       IFTRUEI DOWN                       the key went down
; D 4127 52 04 00 02    ADDXI R4 0002                      the gap loop counts in TWOS: R4 = 2 x gap, no doubling needed
; D 412B 88 4C          TESTGXY R4 >= R12
; D 412D A0 01 3E       IFTRUEI PAST                       past LETTER: the decisions
; D 4130 C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 4131 C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 4132 C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 4133 C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 4134 C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 4135 C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 4136 C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 4137 C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 4138 C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 4139 C0 01          DLYI 01                            one sample
; D 413B B0 01 1A       GAL UL
; PAST:
; D 413E 86 05 00 01    TESTXI R5 0001
; D 4142 A0 01 48       IFTRUEI P1                         nothing keyed, or done already
; D 4145 BD 01 B2       CALL LETTER                        the letter is complete
; P1:
; D 4148 88 49          TESTGXY R4 >= R9
; D 414A A1 01 5A       IFFALSEI P1X                       past WORD:
; D 414D 8C 06          TESTXZ R6
; D 414F A0 01 55       IFTRUEI P2
; D 4152 BD 01 DA       CALL SPACE                           a word gap
; P2:
; D 4155 C0 01          DLYI 01                            one sample
; D 4157 B0 01 1A       GAL UL
; P1X:
; D 415A C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 415B B0 01 55       GAL P2                             padded: every sample of a gap is the same length
; DOWN:
; D 415E 0A 01          SETQ 01                            Q follows the key
; D 4160 23 00 4D       COPYXY R4 -> R13                   RD = the gap that just ended - learned from after this mark
; D 4163 11 04 00 00    LOADXI R4 0000
; DL:
; D 4167 42 04          INCX R4
; D 4169 C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 416A C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 416B C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 416C C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 416D C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 416E C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 416F C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 4170 C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 4171 C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 4172 C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 4173 C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 4174 C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 4175 C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 4176 C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 4177 C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 4178 C0 01          DLYI 01                            one sample
; D 417A 10 00 00       LOADAI 0000
; D 417D 09             GETEFA                             EF1-4 as a mask
; D 417E 1A 08          TESTBITI 08                        EF4: the Input switch
; D 4180 A0 01 67       IFTRUEI DL
; D 4183 0A 00          SETQ 00                            key up
; D 4185 F1 43 00       RUNMC 4300                         learn: the element, dot/dash, the averages, the thresholds
; D 4188 B0 01 16       GAL UP
; TKEY:
; D 418B CB             SERIN
; D 418C 21 07          COPYAX Acc -> R7
; D 418E 86 07 00 71    TESTXI R7 0071
; D 4192 A0 01 A6       IFTRUEI QUIT
; D 4195 86 07 00 51    TESTXI R7 0051
; D 4199 A0 01 A6       IFTRUEI QUIT
; D 419C 86 07 00 1B    TESTXI R7 001B
; D 41A0 A0 01 A6       IFTRUEI QUIT
; D 41A3 B0 01 1A       GAL UL                             anything else: ignored
; QUIT:
; D 41A6 11 0E 08 2F    LOADXI R14 082F
; D 41AA C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 41AC 0A 00          SETQ 00
; D 41AE 00             HALT
; D 41AF F0 00 00       BREAK
; LETTER:
; D 41B2 10 00 2A       LOADAI 002A
; D 41B5 11 07 00 80    LOADXI R7 0080
; D 41B9 89 57          TESTLXY R5 < R7
; D 41BB A1 01 CB       IFFALSEI LP                        too long: *
; D 41BE 2E 05 0C 00    READIDX R5 0C00                    the leading-1 code -> the character
; D 41C2 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000
; D 41C5 A1 01 CB       IFFALSEI LP
; D 41C8 10 00 2A       LOADAI 002A
; LP:
; D 41CB C9             SEROUT
; D 41CC 05 00          OUTA 00                            and on the hex display
; D 41CE 42 08          INCX R8
; D 41D0 11 05 00 01    LOADXI R5 0001
; D 41D4 11 06 00 01    LOADXI R6 0001
; D 41D8 BE 00          RETURN
; SPACE:
; D 41DA 11 06 00 00    LOADXI R6 0000
; D 41DE 11 07 00 40    LOADXI R7 0040
; D 41E2 89 87          TESTLXY R8 < R7
; D 41E4 A1 01 ED       IFFALSEI SNL
; D 41E7 CA 20          SEROUTI 20
; D 41E9 42 08          INCX R8
; D 41EB BE 00          RETURN
; SNL:
; D 41ED 11 08 00 00    LOADXI R8 0000
; D 41F1 CA 0D          SEROUTI 0D
; D 41F3 CA 0A          SEROUTI 0A                         a new line (RE holds a gap average)
; D 41F5 BE 00          RETURN

